; IsaacRecomp mod. Turn it on or off with tools/mod_manager.html (or "mods =" in isaac.ini).
id = challengelab
name = Challenge Lab
version = 1.1
author = IsaacRecomp
category = Gameplay
summary = Up to 8 challenges of your own, on a new page of the challenge list.
engine = challengelab
description = A second page for the challenge list ("To Do List", Wrath of the Lamb and Eternal Edition): an arrow next to Back, like the collection's, turns to the Challenge Lab list, with up to 8 challenges of your own; the same arrow there goes back. Make them with tools/challenge_lab_maker.html, which writes mods/customchallenges.txt: each one has its name, where it ends (Mom, Mom's Heart, Isaac, Satan or The Chest), the character (The Gone too, with his mod on; Isaac without it), the starting items (The Gone's too, with his mod on) and trinket - the character starts with those only -, the rules the game's own challenges use (darkness, the labyrinth or the Lost on every floor, fewer or no treasure rooms, bad luck), Eternal Edition's hard mode, the Curse of the Blind (no tears of your own; familiars still shoot) and, as an advanced option, other base stats (speed, tears, damage, range, shot speed, luck, hearts, pickups). They can all be played from the start, and their runs are runs apart: nothing in them unlocks anything or counts in your statistics, endings, secrets or collection, and the item pools have every item, as if all were unlocked. Finished ones are crossed out (complete = 1 in customchallenges.txt). Eight challenges come with it, from fun to very hard (written into the mods folder when it has no list yet). Works with Continuum (a challenge left and resumed keeps its rules).
